<p>French voters headed to the polls on Sunday for municipal elections across the country, in a contest widely seen as a test of the far right’s momentum and of mainstream parties’ resilience ahead of the 2027 presidential election. Marseille has drawn particular attention, with the far right performing strongly in France’s second-largest city and making the race there a possible bellwether for broader national shifts.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/Ji5gLB07Agk6CZrj2V-ZdDgZ6wTGJsKR__RqWS4ncjbR-KFLdhkRSypDA6VfRJ-r0tG51lzJ9jWEnyn4rkjyDhp3CqL2Q-_HrOQy1_OfJWzQY553e9R7vKdDXMyWu3ZtzfpWlRW7Pp_lgnwDPOl7w9yC8XCLGFTVpb2NjiqpRFMh8zoq6xuoqH2zWGm5kJ29XmetJGO1ahN2MphbkqsSm5MoO7g' alt='Supporters of Benoît Payan, the incumbent mayor of Marseille, distribute leaflets in the city ahead of a tight race featuring a strong far-right candidate.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Urban appeal: A strong far-right result in Marseille would suggest the movement is expanding its reach in a major city, not just building support elsewhere.</li><li>Local legitimacy: Le Monde says candidates have turned local roots into a symbolic asset, using community ties to show they belong in the municipal races they want to win.</li><li>Trusted office: The Hindu describes mayors as France’s most trusted elected officials, helping explain why a local ballot can matter well beyond town hall.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>New York Times analysis: The newspaper describes Marseille’s race as a bellwether for France’s political future because a strong far-right result there would show the movement broadening its urban appeal. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/15/world/europe/france-marseille-mayor-election-far-right.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Le Monde analysis: Le Monde argues that candidates’ efforts to stress their local roots show how much municipal legitimacy in France still depends on being seen as part of the community one hopes to govern. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/opinion/article/2026/03/15/being-a-local-has-become-a-key-selling-point-in-france-s-municipal-elections_6751454_23.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>Financial Times analysis: The Financial Times says the municipal vote is setting the stage for next year’s presidential contest, as the far right tries to turn local gains into national momentum. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/3afde091-d7a2-495f-9d7d-856ca2a50ee5'>Financial Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/15/world/europe/france-marseille-mayor-election-far-right.html'>Marseille’s Tight Mayoral Race Is a Bellwether for France’s Future</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/opinion/article/2026/03/15/being-a-local-has-become-a-key-selling-point-in-france-s-municipal-elections_6751454_23.html'>Being a local has become a key selling point in France&#x27;s municipal elections</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/french-mayoral-elections-gauge-far-right-strength-before-presidential-ballot'>French mayoral elections gauge far-right strength before presidential ballot</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/3afde091-d7a2-495f-9d7d-856ca2a50ee5'>France votes in mayoral elections ahead of 2027 showdown</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/french-mayoral-elections-gauge-far-right-strength-before-presidential-ballot/article70745695.ece'>French Mayoral elections gauge far-right strength before Presidential ballot</a> - thehindu.com</li></ul>